*% Canon LBP-1120 (CAPT) via PostScript: based on Microsoft MSGENBW.PPD (generic grayscale
*% imagesetter) with extra quality options read by the CAPT print script (capt_print_redmon).
*FormatVersion: "4.2"
*FileVersion: "1.2"
*PCFileName: "LBP1120.PPD"
*LanguageVersion: English
*Product: "()"
*PSVersion: "(52.3) 320"
*% Product and PSVersion are meaningless in this generic PPD.
*ModelName: "Canon LBP-1120 (CAPT)"
*NickName: "Canon LBP-1120 (CAPT)"
*ShortNickName: "Canon LBP-1120 (CAPT)"

*% General Information and Defaults ===============
*FreeVM: "175500"
*LanguageLevel: "1"
*% Not a color printer, but tells driver to generate color code.
*ColorDevice: True
*Extensions: FileSystem CMYK
*FileSystem: True

*% Print quality options (same set as the Quality tab of the original Canon driver).
*% The options carry no PostScript code: the CAPT script reads the %%BeginFeature lines.
*% Settings mode: Standard ignores every quality option below (safe defaults from settings.ini),
*% Manual applies them. Windows remembers the choice and the values (per user/application).
*% Short option names on purpose: the Windows settings tree cuts long lines (14.10.2026).
*% Settings mode: Standard ignores the options marked (Manual); Manual applies them. Quick preset works in both modes
*% and overrides the other options. Replaced (resets counter!) resets the cartridge sheet counter - set back to Keep.
*OpenUI *CaptMode/Settings mode: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 19 AnySetup *CaptMode
*DefaultCaptMode: Standard
*CaptMode Standard/Standard (recommended): ""
*CaptMode Manual/Manual: ""
*CloseUI: *CaptMode

*OpenUI *CaptCartridge/Cartridge counter: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 19 AnySetup *CaptCartridge
*DefaultCaptCartridge: Keep
*CaptCartridge Keep/Keep: ""
*CaptCartridge Replaced/Replaced (resets counter!): ""
*CloseUI: *CaptCartridge

*OpenUI *CaptPreset/Quick preset (overrides below): PickOne
*OrderDependency: 19 AnySetup *CaptPreset
*DefaultCaptPreset: None
*CaptPreset None/None: ""
*CaptPreset Text/Text: ""
*CaptPreset Photo/Photo: ""
*CaptPreset Saver/Toner saver: ""
*CaptPreset Draft/Draft: ""
*CloseUI: *CaptPreset

*OpenUI *CaptDuplex/Manual duplex: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 19 AnySetup *CaptDuplex
*DefaultCaptDuplex: Off
*CaptDuplex Off/Off: ""
*CaptDuplex On/On (flip stack like a book): ""
*CloseUI: *CaptDuplex

*OpenUI *Resolution/Resolution (Manual): PickOne
*OrderDependency: 20 AnySetup *Resolution
*DefaultResolution: 600dpi
*Resolution 600dpi/600 dpi: ""
*Resolution 300dpi/300 dpi (fast): ""
*CloseUI: *Resolution

*OpenUI *CaptHalftone/Halftoning (Manual): PickOne
*OrderDependency: 21 AnySetup *CaptHalftone
*DefaultCaptHalftone: Auto
*CaptHalftone Auto/Auto: ""
*CaptHalftone Pattern1/Pattern 1: ""
*CaptHalftone Ordered/Fine pattern: ""
*CaptHalftone Smooth/Smooth: ""
*CaptHalftone None/None (text only): ""
*CloseUI: *CaptHalftone

*OpenUI *CaptDensity/Toner Density (Manual): PickOne
*OrderDependency: 22 AnySetup *CaptDensity
*DefaultCaptDensity: Normal
*CaptDensity Lightest/Lightest: ""
*CaptDensity Light/Light: ""
*CaptDensity Normal/Normal: ""
*CaptDensity Dark/Dark: ""
*CaptDensity Darkest/Darkest: ""
*CloseUI: *CaptDensity

*OpenUI *CaptTonerSaver/Toner Saver (Manual): Boolean
*OrderDependency: 23 AnySetup *CaptTonerSaver
*DefaultCaptTonerSaver: False
*CaptTonerSaver False/Off: ""
*CaptTonerSaver True/On: ""
*CloseUI: *CaptTonerSaver

*OpenUI *CaptRefinement/Image Refinement (Manual): Boolean
*OrderDependency: 24 AnySetup *CaptRefinement
*DefaultCaptRefinement: True
*CaptRefinement False/Off: ""
*CaptRefinement True/On: ""
*CloseUI: *CaptRefinement

*OpenUI *CaptBrightness/Brightness (Manual): PickOne
*OrderDependency: 25 AnySetup *CaptBrightness
*DefaultCaptBrightness: Zero
*CaptBrightness Minus100/-100%: ""
*CaptBrightness Minus90/-90%: ""
*CaptBrightness Minus80/-80%: ""
*CaptBrightness Minus70/-70%: ""
*CaptBrightness Minus60/-60%: ""
*CaptBrightness Minus50/-50%: ""
*CaptBrightness Minus40/-40%: ""
*CaptBrightness Minus30/-30%: ""
*CaptBrightness Minus20/-20%: ""
*CaptBrightness Minus10/-10%: ""
*CaptBrightness Zero/0%: ""
*CaptBrightness Plus10/+10%: ""
*CaptBrightness Plus20/+20%: ""
*CaptBrightness Plus30/+30%: ""
*CaptBrightness Plus40/+40%: ""
*CaptBrightness Plus50/+50%: ""
*CaptBrightness Plus60/+60%: ""
*CaptBrightness Plus70/+70%: ""
*CaptBrightness Plus80/+80%: ""
*CaptBrightness Plus90/+90%: ""
*CaptBrightness Plus100/+100%: ""
*CloseUI: *CaptBrightness

*OpenUI *CaptContrast/Contrast (Manual): PickOne
*OrderDependency: 26 AnySetup *CaptContrast
*DefaultCaptContrast: Zero
*CaptContrast Minus100/-100%: ""
*CaptContrast Minus90/-90%: ""
*CaptContrast Minus80/-80%: ""
*CaptContrast Minus70/-70%: ""
*CaptContrast Minus60/-60%: ""
*CaptContrast Minus50/-50%: ""
*CaptContrast Minus40/-40%: ""
*CaptContrast Minus30/-30%: ""
*CaptContrast Minus20/-20%: ""
*CaptContrast Minus10/-10%: ""
*CaptContrast Zero/0%: ""
*CaptContrast Plus10/+10%: ""
*CaptContrast Plus20/+20%: ""
*CaptContrast Plus30/+30%: ""
*CaptContrast Plus40/+40%: ""
*CaptContrast Plus50/+50%: ""
*CaptContrast Plus60/+60%: ""
*CaptContrast Plus70/+70%: ""
*CaptContrast Plus80/+80%: ""
*CaptContrast Plus90/+90%: ""
*CaptContrast Plus100/+100%: ""
*CloseUI: *CaptContrast

*% Paper Handling ===================
*% These page sizes are not supported by all printers.
*OpenUI *PageSize: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 30 AnySetup *PageSize
*DefaultPageSize: A4
*PageSize A4: "a4"
*PageSize A5: "a5"
*PageSize A6: "a6"
*PageSize A7/A7 (74x105, experimental): "a7"
*CloseUI: *PageSize

*OpenUI *PageRegion: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 40 AnySetup *PageRegion
*DefaultPageRegion: A4
*PageRegion A4: "a4"
*PageRegion A5: "a5"
*PageRegion A6: "a6"
*PageRegion A7/A7 (74x105, experimental): "a7"
*CloseUI: *PageRegion

*% The following entries provide information about specific paper keywords.
*DefaultImageableArea: A4
*% 30.09.2026: real printable area measured on the printer (llx lly urx ury, points, origin = bottom-left).
*% The first ~5 mm of the leading edge cannot be printed (raster starts 120 px @600 dpi below it);
*% 05.10.2026: A4 now also prints 1:1 across the full width (like A5); A4, A5 and custom sizes print 1:1 with a
*% 2 mm clear strip at the left, right and bottom edges.
*ImageableArea A4: "5.7 5.7 589.3 827.6"
*ImageableArea A5: "5.7 5.7 414.3 580.6"
*ImageableArea A6: "5.7 5.7 291.9 404.8"
*ImageableArea A7/A7 (74x105, experimental): "5.7 5.7 204.1 282.9"

*% These provide the physical dimensions of the paper (by keyword)
*DefaultPaperDimension: A4
*PaperDimension A4: "595 842"
*PaperDimension A5: "420 595"
*PaperDimension A6: "298 420"
*PaperDimension A7/A7 (74x105, experimental): "210 298"

*% Custom Page Sizes -- discards HeightOffset, currently doesn't allow WidthOffset
*CustomPageSize True: "exch pop statusdict /setpageparams get exec"
*% 30.09.2026: real printer limits. Windows puts the LONG edge into "Width" (100x150 mm ->
*% Width 425 pt, Height 283 pt), so Width = 127..297 mm, Height = 76..210 mm.
*ParamCustomPageSize Width: 1 points 360 842
*ParamCustomPageSize Height: 2 points 216 595
*ParamCustomPageSize WidthOffset/Margins: 3 points 0 0
*ParamCustomPageSize HeightOffset: 4 points 0 0
*ParamCustomPageSize Orientation: 5 int 0 1

*% This machine is roll-fed or tray handling is limited.
*OpenUI *InputSlot: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 20 AnySetup *InputSlot
*DefaultInputSlot: Cassette
*InputSlot Cassette/Tray: ""
*CloseUI: *InputSlot

*RequiresPageRegion All: True

*% Font Information =====================

*DefaultFont: Courier
*Font Courier: Standard "(001.004)" Standard ROM
*Font Courier-Bold: Standard "(001.004)" Standard ROM
*Font Courier-BoldOblique: Standard "(001.004)" Standard ROM
*Font Courier-Oblique: Standard "(001.004)" Standard ROM
*Font Helvetica: Standard "(001.002)" Standard ROM
*Font Helvetica-Bold: Standard "(001.002)" Standard ROM
*Font Helvetica-BoldOblique: Standard "(001.002)" Standard ROM
*Font Helvetica-Oblique: Standard "(001.002)" Standard ROM
*Font Symbol: Special "(001.003)" Special ROM
*Font Times-Bold: Standard "(001.002)" Standard ROM
*Font Times-BoldItalic: Standard "(001.004)" Standard ROM
*Font Times-Italic: Standard "(001.002)" Standard ROM
*Font Times-Roman: Standard "(001.002)" Standard ROM
